## 4. PM/UM trap reconciliation (decision 3 — no unexplained diffs)

Measured on Egg (x86_64, 4RM x DAZ x FTZ, directed + PRNG corpus),
ref = transcribed upstream generic wrapper, cand = proposed arch.
Default ABI (all traps masked) is the contract surface; unmasked
configurations are debug-only. Table (ref traps / cand traps):

| Mask | nearbyint ref/cand | nearbyintf ref/cand | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| IM (sNaN) | 0 / N | 0 / N | DIFFERENT, accepted per decision 1: cand quiets + raises IE (x86 semantics: roundsd raises invalid on sNaN; payload otherwise preserved — proven bit-exact). Generic is silent. Payload behaviour preserved both sides. IM-unmasked traps documented, not reproduced from generic. |
| DM (denormal, DAZ=0 subnormal) | N / N | N / N | PARITY: both trap via denormal-operand detection (generic toint-add, cand ucomisd). |
| DM (DAZ=1) | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 | PARITY (silent both sides; inputs flushed). |
| UM | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 | PARITY BY ABSENCE: neither implementation can produce a tiny result (generic rint chain is normal-scale throughout; cand has no FP result on the cold path). No quirk to reproduce — unlike F3 floor/ceil, whose generic `- x` op traps here. |
| PM | N / 0 | N / 0 | DIFFERENT, accepted per decision 2: generic raises PE via its toint intermediate (masked: cleared by the wrapper; unmasked: traps). Candidate never raises PE — this is the required nearbyint behaviour, not a gap. Reproducing the trap would require raising PE, which the contract forbids. The function cannot simultaneously "never raise inexact" and "trap on inexact"; masked behaviour (the specified surface) is identical. |
| ZM / OM | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 | PARITY (no division, no overflow possible). |
| ALL | ref = PM-set | cand = IM+DM sets | Consistent with the rows above (first exception wins per call). |

No other (fn, mask, mode) divergence exists in the matrix:
f4diff masked totals are vfails=0 ffails=0 pefails=0 over 97,056
cases, and the sNaN class (4,873 cases) is the sole classified
event, all with payload preserved and quiet-bit-only value delta.

